#analogy-box(title: "Everyday Example — The School Exam Cycle")[
  Teachers *set standards* (the syllabus and the pass marks), *measure* (the
  test papers), *compare* (the marks against the pass line), and *act* —
  extra classes for the topics where the class fell short, or a re-exam when
  the paper itself was unfair. Next term's teaching plan absorbs every lesson.
  A school term is the control cycle, four times a year, with report cards in
  place of dashboards.
]

